From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: use mdelay() for the 5.85 ms rxcore delay

ARM rejects a constant udelay() above 2 ms at link time
(__bad_udelay). The delay may run in atomic context, so keep it busy
waiting with mdelay().

Index: backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
===================================================================
--- backports-7.2.orig/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
+++ backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
@@ -2873,7 +2873,7 @@ static void b43_phy_ac_rxcore_setstate(s
 	 * read after. The capture delays 5848 us after the wide-open write.
 	 */
 	b43_phy_write(dev, 0x16d8, 0xffff);
-	udelay(5850);
+	mdelay(6);
 
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, 0x0160, (u16)~0x0007, coremask);
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, B43_PHY_AC_RF_SEQ_MODE, (u16)~0x0070,
